# File: specs/320-keep-observing-live-review-workers-after-prompt-wait-failure/feature.gherkin
#
# Generated from: specs/320-keep-observing-live-review-workers-after-prompt-wait-failure/requirements.md
Feature: Keep observing live review workers after prompt-wait failure
  The execute controller previously treated a non-stall prompt-wait failure as
  immediate review failure even while the exact owned review worker remained live.
  Review completion now follows validated handoff or confirmed worker disappearance.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Live review worker completes after prompt-wait failure
    Given an exact owned review worker remains listed without a handoff
    And its controller-owned prompt wait returns a non-stall failure
    When that worker later writes a valid artifact-backed review handoff
    Then execute accepts the review and continues the queue
    And it does not stop with review_failed or send stalled-prompt recovery keys

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Missing review worker still fails closed
    Given a non-stall review prompt wait failed without a valid handoff
    When the exact owned review worker is absent or disappears during observation
    Then execute fails the review as review_failed or process_lost
    And it does not recreate the review worker
    And missing review-base and agent_prompt_stalled recovery behavior remain unchanged
